id: pm-k785lu
title: Sentry gate misclassifies handled snapshot identifier validation as a blocking runtime error
description: "The strict release observability gate counts the handled snapshot-name and fingerprint validation CommandError as a high-severity runtime failure, blocking an otherwise green release lane."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:observability","area:release",regression,sentry,telemetry
created_at: "2026-07-29T20:38:39.675Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T20:57:15.450Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-29T20:49:04.080Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-29T20:49:04.080Z"
author: "harness:codex"
parent: pm-5oj5
severity: high
environment: Production Sentry release gate after workspace snapshot acceptance verification
repro_steps: "Run pnpm sentry:telemetry:gate while the unresolved handled snapshot identifier validation event is within the 14-day activity window."
resolution: Added an exact handled-validation allowlist for snapshot identifier input failures without weakening unhandled or unrelated Error gating.
expected_result: Handled user-input validation remains visible as expected-handled evidence and does not consume the zero-high release threshold; unhandled or generic Error events with the same text remain blocking.
actual_result: "Focused regression and live Sentry/telemetry gate pass; live result reports critical=0 high=0 ignored_expected_handled=1, with unhandled and unrelated Error negative controls remaining blocking."
fixed_version: next
regression: true
